  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In 2023 congressional testimony, Paul Dabbar said Chinese hardware and AI algorithms could pose national security risks and recommended banning all chips, software, electric vehicle components, and power grid controls from China. In May 2025 hearing statements, he said broad AI regulation could impede economic progress and that NIST should focus on traditional strengths such as standards and measurement. Also in May 2025, he said that if confirmed he would support continued AI model testing, NIST sharing of results and standards development, and continued U.S. leadership on AI. In December 2025 official-role remarks and a January 2026 reported statement, he said AI can increase manufacturer competitiveness and attract investment in America.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s8",
